## Findings
1. advisory: The draft ran the done-step check after runDone and relied on the existing unwind. runDone refuses a record that is already done ("not building, verifying or review"), and rollback() with nothing staged leaves the working record done. The draft's "a corrected handoff then performs" therefore could not happen. The check now runs before mergeRefusal, the chore branch and runDone, against the working-tree opera with the opus projected {state: done, end: at}; `at` is the same instant passed to runDone as --now. Nothing is written, so there is nothing to unwind. check: packages/cli/src/next.test.ts W-186-b2
2. advisory: The done step must read the working-tree docs/SESSION-HANDOFF.md through readContainedRegularFile. f.handoff is `git show refs/heads/master:docs/SESSION-HANDOFF.md` (next.ts:430), which never holds the producer's edit. check: packages/cli/src/next.test.ts W-186-b2
3. advisory: The Next field now covers any Resume line that opens with the word Next and has a colon on that line, together with its continuation lines. Today's "**Next, in order:**" is checked under it (production lex §11, stricter reading), and the draft's exact "Next:" label would have skipped it. Today's handoff then blocks at line 24, which names done W-197 and W-199. That is correct: next already holds new starts until a retro is filed (W-137 behaviour 4), and check advises retro.overdue. The producer rewords line 24 on master before `branch`; the builder never edits the handoff. check: process.handoff.resume
4. advisory: The draft made an absent handoff a block. That would flip stage-states.test.ts "W-129 behaviour 15: the whole cycle on one branch, with check clean at every step": its fixture is <dir>/studio with repo <dir> and no handoff, and it asserts no block. The draft did not name this row. In check, an absent handoff (ENOENT) now gives no finding, matching performDone's own `f.handoff !== undefined` gate. At done, when master keeps a handoff, an absent working-tree file still holds. This is Default 2. check: packages/cli/src/stage-states.test.ts W-129 behaviour 15
